Subject: [M156] [WebAudio] Stop paused destination and guard automatic pull on
 close

Original change's description:
> [WebAudio] Stop paused destination and guard automatic pull on close
>
> When an AudioContext is closed while its frame is frozen, the platform
> audio destination is in the kPaused state (`IsPlaying()` is false), so
> `StopPlatformDestination()` previously skipped calling `Stop()`. When
> the frame later thawed, `Resume()` restarted the audio thread on the
> closed context, and `Render()` invoked `ProcessAutomaticPullNodes()`
> even when pulling the audio graph was disabled, causing an object
> lifetime issue with disposed upstream nodes.
>
> Changes:
> - Call `platform_destination_->Stop()` in `StopPlatformDestination()`
>   whenever `platform_destination_` is present so `kPaused` destinations
>   transition to `kStopped`.
> - Move `ProcessAutomaticPullNodes()` inside the active graph-pulling
>   branch of `RealtimeAudioDestinationHandler::Render()`.
> - Add `AudioContextTest.CloseWhileFrozenStopsDestination` to verify
>   closing a frozen context stops the destination and guards automatic
>   pull nodes.
>
